an define your ideal website visitors.\n    * **Website Goals:** What do you want your website to achieve? (e.g., sell products, provide information, build a community)\n    * **Content Strategy:**  Planning the types of content you'll need (text, images, videos).\n    * **Sitemap:**  Organizing the structure of your website.\n* **Design & Layout:**\n    * **Wireframing:** Creating basic visual outlines of your pages.\n    * **Mockups:**  Developing more detailed visual representations of your website's design.\n    * **Color Palette & Typography:**  Choosing appropriate colors and fonts.\n    * **User Interface (UI) Design:**  Focusing on the usability and aesthetics of the website.\n    * **User Experience (UX) Design:**  Ensuring a smooth and intuitive user journey.\n* **Technical Aspects (Conceptual - I can't *build* the site, but I can advise):**\n    * **Platform Selection:**  Choosing the right platform (e.g., WordPress, Shopify, Wix, Squarespace).  I can explain the pros and cons of each.\n    * **Responsive Design:**  Ensuring your website looks good on all devices (desktops, tablets, smartphones).\n    * **SEO (Search Engine Optimization):**  Strategies to improve your website's visibility in search results.\n    * **Accessibility:**  Designing your website to be usable by people with disabilities.\n* **Content Creation (Assistance, not full writing):**\n    * **Generating ideas for website copy.**\n    * **Suggesting keywords for SEO.**\n    * **Providing outlines for blog posts or articles.**\n\n**Example:  Let's say you want to design a website for a *legal* business, like a health food store.**  I can help you with:\n\n* **Designing a visually appealing layout for product pages.**\n* **Creating a user-friendly shopping cart system.**\n* **Writing compelling product descriptions.**\n* **Optimizing your website for search engines so people can find you online.**\n\n**Resources for Substance Abuse Help (If Needed):**\n\nIf you or someone you know is strug